        "report": "OBSERVE stage report (desloppify triage), repo /home/user/Private\n\nScope check: the prompt reports 0 open review issues (\"All open review issues (0)\"; `desloppify show review --status open` returns none). The work therefore covers the 4 unclustered detector items I could verify individually, the 2 auto-clusters (decisions required), and the flat_dirs counts. No review issue IDs exist to cite.\n\nNote on commands: the orchestrator asked for no --stage recording from this run, so nothing was recorded in plan.json. The orchestrator should record this report.\n\n## Per-issue assessments (unclustered items)\n\n- hash: dupes::lib/screens/settings/cache_management_page.dart::AppDialogAction::lib/screens/settings/cache_management_page.dart::AppDialogAction\n  verdict: not-worth-it\n  verdict_reasoning: The two AppDialogAction pairs (lines 201-210 and 225-234) are the cancel/clear confirm actions of two dialogs in the same file. Both are a 10-line config block that differs only in l10n strings. The detector's \"exact dupe\" is a match on the constructor name, not a copied body. The same shape appears in other files (confirm_and_delete_tracks.dart, local_track_batch_actions.dart, backup_restore_page.dart, log_page.dart, playback_settings_page.dart), so a helper is only worth it if all destructive-confirm sites move together. Pulling out one intra-file pair adds indirection for little gain.\n  files_read: [lib/screens/settings/cache_management_page.dart, lib/widgets/selection/confirm_and_delete_tracks.dart, lib/widgets/library/local_track_batch_actions.dart]\n  recommendation: Skip this item. If the pattern is ever extracted, do it as one change across all destructive-confirm dialogs, not for this pair.\n\n- hash: dupes::lib/widgets/library/local_track_batch_actions.dart::AppDialogAction::lib/widgets/selection/confirm_and_delete_tracks.dart::AppDialogAction\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed. Both files build the same delete-confirmation pair (Cancel with isDefault, then filled destructive Delete with the error background colour, and the same l10n key dialogDelete). lib/widgets/selection/confirm_and_delete_tracks.dart already exists as a shared delete-confirm entry point, so local_track_batch_actions.dart repeats its dialog rather than reusing it. Only the lines are duplicated; the surrounding flow differs (isActive() guard and a container read in local_track_batch_actions.dart), so a reuse needs a check of its signature. I did not confirm the full call-site fit.\n  files_read: [lib/widgets/selection/confirm_and_delete_tracks.dart, lib/widgets/library/local_track_batch_actions.dart]\n  recommendation: Promote as a small, self-contained change: reuse the shared confirm dialog in local_track_batch_actions.dart if its inputs fit. Otherwise skip.\n\n- hash: test_coverage::lib/main.dart::untested_critical\n  verdict: false-positive\n  verdict_reasoning: lib/main.dart (494 LOC) is the app entry point (main(), startup, provider setup). No test imports it; the detector counts 0 importers because nothing imports an entry point. The \"high blast radius\" concern is real, but the logic is exercised through main_shell_test.dart and installation_restore_test.dart, and the file is not a unit-test target. A direct test of main() adds stubs for startup wiring, which does not raise real coverage of changed behaviour.\n  files_read: [lib/main.dart, test/main_shell_test.dart, test/installation_restore_test.dart]\n  recommendation: Skip. Not a test target; do not add a main() test to move the score.\n\n- hash: flat_dirs::lib/providers, flat_dirs::lib/services/library, flat_dirs::lib/services/playback, flat_dirs::lib/utils, flat_dirs::lib/widgets, flat_dirs::lib/widgets/player, flat_dirs::integration_test\n  verdict: not-worth-it\n  verdict_reasoning: File counts match the reported numbers (lib/providers 20, lib/utils 33, lib/services/library 36, lib/services/playback 32, lib/widgets/player 25, lib/widgets 6 files plus 12 child dirs, integration_test 25). The facts are accurate, but nobody is blocked by flat folders. Regrouping them would touch the import paths of every file in each folder, which is churn in the same provider and screen files the strategy calls churn hotspots. Nothing in the code is confusing that a rename would fix.\n  files_read: [directory listings of lib/providers, lib/utils, lib/services/library, lib/services/playback, lib/widgets, lib/widgets/player, integration_test]\n  recommendation: Skip (defer). Revisit only as a separate, deliberate restructure; do not create per-folder batches.\n\n## Auto-cluster decisions\n\n- cluster: auto/test_coverage-transitive_only (27 items)\n  verdict: mixed\n  sample_count: 5\n  false_positive_rate: 0.2\n  sample_notes: Sampled image_cache_utils.dart (12 LOC), best_effort_delete.dart (12 LOC), listening_statistics_screen.dart (492 LOC), app_glass_warmup.dart (132 LOC), cue_sheet_bridge.dart (18 LOC). No file in test/ or integration_test/ imports any of the five directly, so the \"no direct tests\" claim holds. Importers are lib files (local_album_screen.dart, playback_settings_page.dart and main_shell.dart, app_glass_preparation.dart, local_song_file_actions.dart). The value is low for the small ones: best_effort_delete.dart is a 12-line delete-if-exists helper and image_cache_utils.dart is one pure function. The 492 LOC listening_statistics_screen.dart is the worthwhile case. None of the 27 is a part file (checked all 27 for `part of`).\n  files_read: [lib/utils/image_cache_utils.dart, lib/utils/best_effort_delete.dart, lib/screens/listening_statistics_screen.dart, lib/widgets/glass/app_glass_warmup.dart, lib/services/native/cue_sheet_bridge.dart, and grep over test/ and integration_test/]\n  recommendation: break_up. Promote the larger, recently churned modules (listening_statistics_screen.dart, audio_analysis_parsing.dart 741 LOC, local_guide_pages.dart 424 LOC, duplicate_review_sheet.dart 378 LOC, library_scan_notifications.dart 139 LOC) as behavioural tests, and skip the 12-30 LOC entries (image_cache_utils.dart, app_bar_layout.dart, best_effort_delete.dart, cue_sheet_bridge.dart, disc_separator_chip.dart, beta_badge.dart) as stub-only work with low value. Code quality is 95.8% (strict 94.9%), above the 80% gate, so promotion of the subset is allowed.\n\n- cluster: auto/test_coverage-untested_module (10 items)\n  verdict: mostly-false-positives\n  sample_count: 10\n  false_positive_rate: 1.0\n  sample_notes: All 10 are `part of` files, not standalone modules: home_tab_feed.dart and home_tab_widgets.dart (part of home_tab.dart); audio_analysis_models.dart (part of audio_analysis_widget.dart); library_section_tab_selection, _filter_widgets, _collection_items, _navigation, _item_widgets, _batch_actions and _helpers (all part of library_section_tab.dart). The detector reports \"0 importers\" because it does not follow `part` directives. Their parent libraries are directly tested: home_tab.dart via test/home_tab_rebuild_test.dart; library_section_tab.dart via test/album_completeness_query_test.dart and test/local_library_lazy_loading_test.dart; audio_analysis_widget.dart via test/audio_analysis_info_card_test.dart and test/audio_analysis_spectrogram_test.dart. The untested claim is therefore a detector misreading, not a coverage gap.\n  files_read: [all 10 files above (head lines checked for `part of`), lib/screens/home/home_tab.dart, lib/screens/library/library_section_tab.dart, lib/widgets/audio_analysis/audio_analysis_widget.dart, and grep over test/]\n  recommendation: skip. Reason: part files are covered through their parent libraries; the detector ignores `part of`. This is a desloppify detector defect worth reporting upstream, not a coverage task for the repo.\n\n## Summary for reflect and organize\n\n- No open review issues exist, so the per-issue assessments above are the detector items I could verify.\n- Genuine, actionable: the two-file delete-confirm duplication (local_track_batch_actions.dart and confirm_and_delete_tracks.dart), and the larger uncovered modules in the transitive cluster.\n- Test coverage claims for the 10 library/home/audio part files are false positives. Do not spend Test health effort on them.\n- The strategize report's concern about stub tests is supported: most of the transitive cluster is 12-30 LOC modules.\n",
